__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"extraExercises",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"extraExercisesEnglish",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const o={'06':{number:'06',storageKey:'lab.tool-off.completed',chapter:'CAP\xcdTULO 2',topic:'USO DE FERRAMENTAS',title:'A ferramenta precisava estar sempre ligada?',summary:'Uma repeti\xe7\xe3o controlada comparou a mesma pergunta com a ferramenta de consulta a documentos ativada e desativada.',context:'O modelo recebia cinco trechos recuperados. A ferramenta de consulta ao documento completo era sempre inclu\xedda, mesmo quando a resposta j\xe1 estava nos trechos.',hypothesisTitle:'HIP\xd3TESE TEST\xc1VEL',hypothesis:'Se a ferramenta causar o comportamento incorreto, remov\xea-la dever\xe1 mudar o resultado, mantendo iguais a pergunta, o contexto e a instru\xe7\xe3o enviada ao modelo.',evidence:[{title:'FERRAMENTA ATIVADA \xb7 10/10',detail:'O modelo emitiu uma chamada de ferramenta e nenhum texto de resposta, inclusive no caso de controle.'},{title:'FERRAMENTA DESATIVADA \xb7 10/10',detail:'O modelo respondeu diretamente e corretamente, citando o trecho [1], inclusive em duas perguntas que havia recusado durante o uso real.'},{title:'TEMPERATURA',detail:'Usar a temperatura padr\xe3o (0,7) ou zero n\xe3o alterou os dois padr\xf5es observados.'}],question:'Qual conclus\xe3o \xe9 sustentada por esta repeti\xe7\xe3o?',choices:[{label:'Disponibilizar a ferramenta alterou o comportamento nesses casos, embora o contexto recuperado j\xe1 fosse suficiente.',correct:!0,feedback:'Isso. O comportamento mudou de forma consistente entre a ferramenta ativada e desativada nos cinco casos repetidos.'},{label:'A repeti\xe7\xe3o demonstra que disponibilizar essa ferramenta causa o mesmo comportamento em qualquer modelo e cole\xe7\xe3o de documentos, tornando desnecess\xe1ria uma compara\xe7\xe3o em outros contextos.',correct:!1,feedback:'A repeti\xe7\xe3o usou um modelo, um conjunto de documentos e cinco casos. Isso n\xe3o permite generalizar para todos os sistemas.'}],decision:'Deixar de oferecer a ferramenta por padr\xe3o. Oferec\xea-la somente quando uma verifica\xe7\xe3o simples indicar que \xe9 necess\xe1rio consultar o documento completo, como em pedidos de resumo. Em uma nova execu\xe7\xe3o com dez perguntas originais, o sistema respondeu corretamente \xe0s seis que podiam ser respondidas e recusou as quatro que exigiam informa\xe7\xf5es de outros departamentos.',limits:'Foi repetida uma \xfanica intera\xe7\xe3o, sem reproduzir um ciclo real de uso da ferramenta no aplicativo. Usaram-se um modelo e documentos curtos com t\xedtulos em negrito. O resultado sustenta a mudan\xe7a nesses casos, mas n\xe3o estabelece uma regra universal para ferramentas.'},'07':{number:'07',storageKey:'lab.prompt-refinement.completed',chapter:'CAP\xcdTULO 2',topic:'INSTRU\xc7\xd5ES AO MODELO E AVALIA\xc7\xc3O',title:'Uma instru\xe7\xe3o mais rigorosa ajudou?',summary:'O teste seguinte comparou, em etapas separadas, uma instru\xe7\xe3o de verifica\xe7\xe3o mais detalhada com a vers\xe3o atual.',context:'A proposta era descrever explicitamente os modos de falha na instru\xe7\xe3o para reduzir a toler\xe2ncia do verificador. O experimento n\xe3o combinou essa mudan\xe7a com a estrat\xe9gia de contexto m\xednimo.',hypothesisTitle:'O QUE SERIA UM EFEITO?',hypothesis:'A hip\xf3tese seria confirmada se as classifica\xe7\xf5es melhorassem nos casos que a nova instru\xe7\xe3o pretendia corrigir.',evidence:[{title:'48 CHAMADAS',detail:'Seis casos \xd7 duas instru\xe7\xf5es \xd7 quatro repeti\xe7\xf5es, com temperatura zero.'},{title:'NENHUMA CLASSIFICA\xc7\xc3O MUDOU',detail:'Todas as combina\xe7\xf5es de caso e instru\xe7\xe3o se repetiram nas quatro tentativas; cada vers\xe3o acertou 12 de 24 casos.'},{title:'A INSTRU\xc7\xc3O QUASE DOBROU DE TAMANHO',detail:'A m\xe9dia passou de 155,5 para 304,5 tokens, um aumento de 96%.'}],question:'O que os resultados recomendam fazer com essa revis\xe3o da instru\xe7\xe3o?',choices:[{label:'Implementar a revis\xe3o porque a instru\xe7\xe3o mais longa descreve melhor os modos de falha e deve tornar o verificador mais rigoroso, mesmo sem altera\xe7\xe3o das classifica\xe7\xf5es observadas.',correct:!1,feedback:'O experimento n\xe3o observou melhora nas classifica\xe7\xf5es. Uma expectativa geral n\xe3o substitui o resultado medido.'},{label:'Descartar esta vers\xe3o: ela n\xe3o mudou as classifica\xe7\xf5es e quase dobrou o tamanho da instru\xe7\xe3o nos casos testados.',correct:!0,feedback:'Isso. A hip\xf3tese foi testada isoladamente, nenhuma classifica\xe7\xe3o mudou e a decis\xe3o registrada foi descartar a revis\xe3o.'}],decision:'A revis\xe3o foi descartada. O resultado \xe9 um lembrete pr\xe1tico: instru\xe7\xf5es adicionais podem aumentar o custo de processamento da entrada sem alterar a avalia\xe7\xe3o do modelo.',limits:'Foi usado um modelo, uma formula\xe7\xe3o e seis casos preparados para o experimento. O resultado n\xe3o prova que toda instru\xe7\xe3o detalhada falhar\xe1; mostra que esta revis\xe3o n\xe3o teve efeito mensur\xe1vel neste conjunto.'},'08':{number:'08',storageKey:'lab.prompt-latency.completed',chapter:'CAP\xcdTULO 3',topic:'LAT\xcaNCIA E MEDI\xc7\xc3O',title:'Uma instru\xe7\xe3o mais longa sempre demora mais?',summary:'Quatro chamadas com contextos semelhantes tiveram tempos bem diferentes. O tamanho da instru\xe7\xe3o, sozinho, permitiu prever a dura\xe7\xe3o?',context:'Cada chamada de verifica\xe7\xe3o, com o contexto completo, foi executada uma vez em um modelo local, com temperatura zero, em uma m\xe1quina equipada apenas com CPU.',hypothesisTitle:'LEIA OS QUATRO PARES',hypothesis:'Se o tamanho da instru\xe7\xe3o, sozinho, previsse a dura\xe7\xe3o das chamadas, as instru\xe7\xf5es um pouco maiores deveriam ser sempre mais lentas.',evidence:[{title:'475 TOKENS \xb7 4,21 s',detail:'Uma chamada de verifica\xe7\xe3o.'},{title:'485 TOKENS \xb7 4,49 s',detail:'Outra chamada, com 10 tokens a mais.'},{title:'495 TOKENS \xb7 1,49 s',detail:'Instru\xe7\xe3o mais longa, mas chamada bem mais r\xe1pida.'},{title:'516 TOKENS \xb7 2,19 s',detail:'A chamada com a maior instru\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o foi a mais lenta.'}],question:'Qual leitura \xe9 mais cuidadosa?',choices:[{label:'Nesta amostra, o tamanho da instru\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o previu a dura\xe7\xe3o; a causa da varia\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o foi medida.',correct:!0,feedback:'Isso. O registro sugere poss\xedveis fatores, mas n\xe3o mediu a causa da varia\xe7\xe3o.'},{label:'A varia\xe7\xe3o observada demonstra que o modelo \xe9 imprevis\xedvel e que o tamanho da entrada n\xe3o afeta a lat\xeancia; portanto, essa vari\xe1vel pode ser exclu\xedda das pr\xf3ximas medi\xe7\xf5es.',correct:!1,feedback:'Quatro chamadas isoladas n\xe3o demonstram isso. O tamanho influencia o processamento total, mas n\xe3o explicou sozinho a varia\xe7\xe3o observada.'}],decision:'Nenhuma mudan\xe7a de sistema foi feita a partir dessas quatro chamadas. O registro serve para mostrar por que uma \xfanica lat\xeancia isolada, sem metadados, n\xe3o deve virar expectativa de desempenho.',limits:'Foram feitas quatro execu\xe7\xf5es isoladas, uma por instru\xe7\xe3o. A carga da m\xe1quina, o cache e a vers\xe3o do ambiente de execu\xe7\xe3o, o equipamento e as diferen\xe7as entre os casos n\xe3o foram medidos. Portanto, n\xe3o \xe9 um teste de desempenho.'},'09':{number:'09',storageKey:'lab.deploy-constraints.completed',chapter:'CAP\xcdTULO 4',topic:'IMPLANTA\xc7\xc3O E RESTRI\xc7\xd5ES',title:'Quando o limite de mem\xf3ria decide',summary:'O servi\xe7o gratuito dispon\xedvel tinha limite de 512 MB e n\xe3o oferecia GPU. O que a equipe precisou mudar \u2014 e que efeito colateral surgiu?',context:'A demonstra\xe7\xe3o precisava funcionar em um servi\xe7o gratuito limitado a 512 MB. Executar o modelo de conversa localmente exigiria v\xe1rios gigabytes para armazenar seus pesos; por isso, essa op\xe7\xe3o foi descartada antes da implanta\xe7\xe3o.',hypothesisTitle:'DECIS\xc3O SOB UMA RESTRI\xc7\xc3O R\xcdGIDA',hypothesis:'A pergunta n\xe3o era qual op\xe7\xe3o tinha melhor qualidade. Era qual forma de execu\xe7\xe3o cabia no limite de mem\xf3ria do servi\xe7o dispon\xedvel.',evidence:[{title:'MODELO DE CONVERSA LOCAL',detail:'Sem GPU e com pesos de v\xe1rios gigabytes, o modelo n\xe3o cabia no plano de 512 MB.'},{title:'VETORIZA\xc7\xc3O LOCAL',detail:'Mesmo com um arquivo de cerca de 90 MB, duas tentativas foram encerradas porque o modelo ultrapassou o limite de mem\xf3ria ao ser carregado.'},{title:'MUDAN\xc7A NA DIMENS\xc3O DOS VETORES',detail:'O servi\xe7o de vetoriza\xe7\xe3o na nuvem produzia vetores com 1.024 dimens\xf5es, em vez de 384. Foi necess\xe1rio recriar a estrutura do banco de dados e os dados da demonstra\xe7\xe3o.'}],question:'Qual conclus\xe3o melhor explica a decis\xe3o e seu impacto?',choices:[{label:'O servi\xe7o na nuvem foi escolhido porque cabia no limite; a troca do modelo de vetoriza\xe7\xe3o tamb\xe9m exigiu recriar a estrutura do banco de dados e os dados.',correct:!0,feedback:'Isso. O limite eliminou a op\xe7\xe3o local nesse plano. A dimens\xe3o dos vetores precisa corresponder ao formato definido no banco de dados.'},{label:'O uso do servi\xe7o na nuvem comprova que ele \xe9 mais r\xe1pido, barato e preciso que a alternativa local, permitindo adotar essa compara\xe7\xe3o como crit\xe9rio suficiente para outras tarefas e provedores.',correct:!1,feedback:'N\xe3o houve compara\xe7\xe3o de qualidade, tempo de resposta ou custo entre as op\xe7\xf5es.'}],decision:'A demonstra\xe7\xe3o passou a usar servi\xe7os na nuvem para conversa e vetoriza\xe7\xe3o. O sistema principal manteve a execu\xe7\xe3o local. A dimens\xe3o dos vetores foi tratada como parte do formato dos dados, e n\xe3o como um detalhe que pudesse ser trocado sem ajustes.',limits:'Foi avaliada uma restri\xe7\xe3o de implanta\xe7\xe3o e feitas duas tentativas de vetoriza\xe7\xe3o local. N\xe3o houve compara\xe7\xe3o de qualidade, tempo de resposta ou custo entre modelos locais e modelos na nuvem.'},10:{number:'10',storageKey:'lab.hosted-fallback.completed',chapter:'CAP\xcdTULO 4',topic:'SERVI\xc7OS NA NUVEM',title:'O que \xe9 preciso para usar um servi\xe7o de IA na nuvem?',summary:'Al\xe9m de escolher o modelo, foi preciso decidir como lidar com contas, cr\xe9ditos, erros e dados enviados a servi\xe7os na nuvem.',context:'O sistema passou a oferecer servi\xe7os na nuvem como alternativa quando o modelo local n\xe3o resolvia o caso. A regra de privacidade permitia enviar apenas a pergunta, nunca os documentos, e exigia autoriza\xe7\xe3o expl\xedcita a cada chamada.',hypothesisTitle:'MODELO OU OPERA\xc7\xc3O?',hypothesis:'Ao conectar um provedor, disponibilidade da conta, credenciais, dados enviados e erros passam a influenciar se a chamada pode ocorrer.',evidence:[{title:'CONTA E CR\xc9DITOS',detail:'Uma chave autenticava, mas a conta n\xe3o tinha cr\xe9ditos. Outro provedor virou padr\xe3o por ser o \xfanico validado de ponta a ponta naquele momento.'},{title:'TRATAMENTO DE ERROS',detail:'Antes de tratamento expl\xedcito, falta de chave ou cr\xe9ditos esgotados chegava como erro gen\xe9rico de servidor.'},{title:'FRONTEIRA DOS DADOS',detail:'A pol\xedtica foi definida para enviar s\xf3 a pergunta e pedir consentimento a cada chamada; nenhum documento seria enviado.'},{title:'RECURSO INACESS\xcdVEL',detail:'Um teste funcional confirmou que a alternativa estava implementada, mas na vers\xe3o local testada n\xe3o havia como o usu\xe1rio acess\xe1-la.'}],question:'Quais itens s\xe3o necess\xe1rios para operar esse servi\xe7o, mas n\xe3o s\xe3o caracter\xedsticas do modelo?',choices:[{label:'Conta, cr\xe9ditos, chaves de acesso, tratamento de falhas e regras para os dados enviados.',correct:!0,feedback:'Isso. Esses fatores determinam se o servi\xe7o pode ser chamado e como a integra\xe7\xe3o se comporta.'},{label:'A qualidade medida do modelo e a compara\xe7\xe3o de lat\xeancia entre provedores, pois os requisitos de integra\xe7\xe3o registrados j\xe1 demonstram qual servi\xe7o apresenta o melhor desempenho na tarefa.',correct:!1,feedback:'O registro n\xe3o comparou qualidade nem lat\xeancia entre provedores; esses dados n\xe3o foram medidos.'}],decision:'A integra\xe7\xe3o passou a lidar com indisponibilidades de forma controlada, pedir autoriza\xe7\xe3o antes de cada chamada e enviar somente a pergunta. Para usar esse servi\xe7o, tamb\xe9m \xe9 preciso que ele esteja acess\xedvel na interface.',limits:'As observa\xe7\xf5es descrevem integra\xe7\xf5es espec\xedficas. As vers\xf5es dos modelos, a dura\xe7\xe3o e o custo de cada chamada n\xe3o foram registrados; portanto, n\xe3o permitem comparar a confiabilidade geral dos provedores.'}},t={'06':{chapter:'CHAPTER 2',topic:'TOOL USE',title:'Did the tool need to stay on?',summary:'A controlled replay compared the same question with the document tool enabled and disabled.',context:'The model received five retrieved passages. The full-document lookup tool was always attached, even when the answer was already in the passages.',hypothesisTitle:'TESTABLE HYPOTHESIS',hypothesis:'If the tool caused the incorrect behavior, removing it should change the result while keeping the question, context, and prompt the same.',evidence:[{title:'TOOL ON \xb7 10/10',detail:'The model made a tool call and returned no answer text, including for the control case.'},{title:'TOOL OFF \xb7 10/10',detail:'The model answered directly and correctly, citing passage [1], including two questions it had refused during live use.'},{title:'TEMPERATURE',detail:'Neither the default temperature (0.7) nor zero changed the two observed patterns.'}],question:'What conclusion is supported by this replay?',choices:[{label:'Offering the tool changed behavior in these cases, even though the retrieved context was sufficient.',correct:!0,feedback:'That is right. Behavior changed consistently between ON and OFF across the five reproduced cases.'},{label:'The replay establishes that offering this tool causes the same behavior in every model and document collection, making comparisons in other operating contexts unnecessary.',correct:!1,feedback:'The replay used one model, one corpus, and five cases. It cannot support a general claim about all systems.'}],decision:'Stop offering the tool by default. Offer it only when a low-cost check indicates that the full document is needed, such as for a summary request. A new live run of ten original questions answered the six answerable questions correctly and refused the four that crossed departments.',limits:'Single-turn replay: it does not reproduce a real tool round trip in the application. One model and short documents with bold headings. The result supports a change for these cases, not a universal rule about tools.'},'07':{chapter:'CHAPTER 2',topic:'PROMPTING AND EVALUATION',title:'Did a stricter prompt help?',summary:'The follow-up compared a more detailed verification prompt with the current one, testing them separately.',context:'The proposal was to spell out failure modes in the prompt to make the verifier less lenient. The experiment did not combine this change with the minimum-context strategy.',hypothesisTitle:'WHAT WOULD COUNT AS AN EFFECT?',hypothesis:'The hypothesis would be supported if verdicts changed in the right direction on the cases the new prompt was intended to fix.',evidence:[{title:'48 CALLS',detail:'Six cases \xd7 two prompts \xd7 four repetitions, at temperature zero.'},{title:'NO VERDICT CHANGED',detail:'Every case-prompt combination was stable in 4/4 runs; both prompts got 12 of 24 cases right.'},{title:'PROMPT NEARLY DOUBLED',detail:'The average grew from 155.5 to 304.5 tokens, a 96% increase.'}],question:'What do the results recommend for this prompt revision?',choices:[{label:'Implement the revision because a longer instruction describes failure modes more fully and should therefore make the verifier stricter, even when the observed verdicts did not change.',correct:!1,feedback:'The experiment observed no improvement in verdicts. A general expectation does not replace the measured result.'},{label:'Discard this revision: it did not change verdicts and nearly doubled the prompt in the tested cases.',correct:!0,feedback:'That is right. The hypothesis was tested in isolation, no verdict changed, and the recorded decision was to discard it.'}],decision:'The revision was discarded. The result is a practical reminder: additional instructions can increase input cost without changing the model\u2019s judgment.',limits:'One model, one wording, and six constructed cases. The result does not prove that every detailed prompt will fail; it shows that this revision had no measurable effect on this set.'},'08':{chapter:'CHAPTER 3',topic:'LATENCY AND MEASUREMENT',title:'Does a longer prompt always take longer?',summary:'Four replays with similar contexts produced very different latencies. Was prompt size alone enough to predict time?',context:'Verification calls with full context were each replayed once on a CPU-only host using a local model at temperature zero.',hypothesisTitle:'COMPARE THE FOUR PAIRS',hypothesis:'If prompt size alone predicted latency in these runs, slightly larger prompts should consistently be slower.',evidence:[{title:'475 TOKENS \xb7 4.21 s',detail:'One verification call.'},{title:'485 TOKENS \xb7 4.49 s',detail:'A different call, with 10 more tokens.'},{title:'495 TOKENS \xb7 1.49 s',detail:'A larger prompt with much lower latency.'},{title:'516 TOKENS \xb7 2.19 s',detail:'The largest prompt was not the slowest call.'}],question:'Which interpretation is more careful?',choices:[{label:'In this sample, prompt size alone did not predict latency; the reason for the variation was not measured.',correct:!0,feedback:'That is right. The record suggests possible factors, but did not measure the cause of the variation.'},{label:'The observed variation establishes that the model is unpredictable and input size does not affect latency, so that variable can be excluded from subsequent measurements.',correct:!1,feedback:'Four isolated calls cannot show that. Input size matters to total work, but it did not explain the observed variation on its own.'}],decision:'No system change was made based on these four calls. The record shows why a single isolated latency, without metadata, should not become a performance expectation.',limits:'Four isolated runs, one per prompt. Host load, runtime cache, version, hardware, and differences between cases were not measured; this is not a benchmark.'},'09':{chapter:'CHAPTER 4',topic:'DEPLOYMENT AND CONSTRAINTS',title:'When the memory limit decides',summary:'A free deployment had 512 MB and no GPU. What did the team need to change\u2014and what side effect followed?',context:'The demo had to run on a free service capped at 512 MB. Local chat inference required several gigabytes for model weights, so the project ruled it out before deployment.',hypothesisTitle:'A DECISION UNDER A HARD CONSTRAINT',hypothesis:'The question was not which option had the best quality. It was which execution mode fit the service\u2019s memory limit.',evidence:[{title:'LOCAL CHAT',detail:'Without a GPU and with multi-gigabyte weights, it did not fit the 512 MB plan.'},{title:'LOCAL EMBEDDING',detail:'Even with a roughly 90 MB file, two attempts were terminated after exceeding the limit while loading the model.'},{title:'A CHANGE IN DIMENSION',detail:'Hosted embeddings produced 1,024-dimensional vectors instead of 384; the database schema and demo data had to be recreated.'}],question:'Which conclusion best explains the decision and its impact?',choices:[{label:'Hosted deployment was chosen because it fit the constraint; changing embeddings also required rebuilding the schema and data.',correct:!0,feedback:'That is right. The constraint ruled out the local option on this plan; vector dimensions tied the model to the stored data format.'},{label:'Using the hosted service establishes that it is faster, cheaper and more accurate than the local alternative, making this comparison sufficient for other tasks and providers.',correct:!1,feedback:'No comparison of quality, latency, or cost between the options was performed.'}],decision:'The demo moved to hosted inference for chat and embeddings. The main system kept local inference. Vector dimensions were treated as part of the data contract, not as an interchangeable detail.',limits:'One deployment constraint and two attempts at local embeddings. There was no comparison of quality, latency, or cost between local and hosted models.'},10:{chapter:'CHAPTER 4',topic:'HOSTED FALLBACK',title:'What comes with a fallback?',summary:'Adding hosted providers brought account, credit, error-handling, and data-boundary decisions along with the model.',context:'The system added hosted providers as an explicit fallback for cases the local model could not handle. The privacy rule allowed sending only the question, never documents, and required explicit confirmation for every call.',hypothesisTitle:'MODEL OR OPERATIONS?',hypothesis:'When a provider is connected, account availability, credentials, data sent, and errors all affect whether the call can happen.',evidence:[{title:'ACCOUNT AND CREDITS',detail:'One key authenticated, but the account had no credits. Another provider became the default because it was the only one validated end to end at that time.'},{title:'ERROR HANDLING',detail:'Before explicit handling was added, a missing key or exhausted credits surfaced as a generic server error.'},{title:'DATA BOUNDARY',detail:'The policy was to send only the question and ask for consent on every call; no document would be sent.'},{title:'INACCESSIBLE PATH',detail:'A functional test found the fallback implemented, but with no user-accessible path in the local deployment that was tested.'}],question:'Which items are operational dependencies of the fallback, rather than model properties?',choices:[{label:'Account, credits, keys, failure handling, and the policy for data sent.',correct:!0,feedback:'That is right. These factors affect whether the service can be called and how the integration behaves.'},{label:'Measured model quality and provider latency comparisons, because the recorded integration requirements already establish which service performs best on the task.',correct:!1,feedback:'The record did not compare model quality or provider latency; those data were not measured.'}],decision:'The integration adopted controlled handling for outages, explicit consent before public calls, and sending only the question. The path also needs to be accessible in the interface for the fallback to be usable.',limits:'These observations describe specific integrations. Model versions, latency, and per-call cost were not recorded, so they cannot compare providers\u2019 overall reliability.'}}},777,[]);
